# "When you remove the last intervention counter" triggers however its controller removes it (its ruling), not only by its
# upkeep ability. Bot1 casts Divine Intervention on turn 1 (a Swamp played for one of its eight mana), it loses a counter in
# Bot1's turn 3 upkeep, and then Bot1's own Vampire Hexmage removes the last one in Bot1's turn 3 main phase - Bot1 the
# controller of that ability (CR 608.2c) - so the game is a draw at once (CR 104.4c), still in that main phase.

[Bot1 Deck]
Divine Intervention
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Swamp
Vampire Hexmage
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

